<section class="section">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:760px">
    <div class="text-center">
      <span class="section-label">Common questions about sign-up</span>
      <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-inline:auto">Quick answers</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Why this order? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">The agreement sets the rules first. Payment comes next, because work begins when your first payment clears. Onboarding comes last, once we're both committed.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if I've already had a discovery call? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">The steps are the same. The call only settles whether we're a good fit.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Why Stripe? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Stripe is a standard payment processor. It meets the card industry's security standard (PCI), so I never see or store your card number, and it handles failed payments, disputes, and Canadian payments.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if I sign the agreement but don't pay right away? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Nothing breaks. The first payment, not the signature, starts the work, so you can sign today and pay tomorrow.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Can I buy the code outright later? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">No. On the monthly plan, I own the code, and there's no code buyout or export of the site. Your domain is registered in your name, and you control it. If you cancel, I help you move it to a registrar of your choice, and the website goes offline at the end of the term.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if I need a refund? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">If you change your mind before I start building, I refund your first payment in full, whenever you ask. Once the build has started, the first payment isn't refundable. The <a href="/agreement/" class="inline-link">service agreement</a> says the same.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

